{"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Property","symbolKind":"property","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"divisions","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLPositiveDivisions","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL20MXLPositiveDivisionsV"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLAttributesV9divisionsAA20MXLPositiveDivisionsVSgvp","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"title":"divisions"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAttributes\/divisions","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlattributes\/divisions"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Musical notation duration is commonly represented as fractions. The divisions element indicates how many"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"divisions per quarter note are used to indicate a note’s duration. For example, if duration = 1 and divisions"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"= 2, this is an eighth note duration. Duration and divisions are used directly for generating sound output, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"they must be chosen to take tuplets into account. Using a divisions element lets us use just one number to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"represent a duration for each note in the score, while retaining the full power of a fractional"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"representation. If maximum compatibility with Standard MIDI 1.0 files is important, do not have the divisions"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value exceed 16383."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAttributes"]]},"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"divisions","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLPositiveDivisions","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPositiveDivisions","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL20MXLPositiveDivisionsV"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps to a nested MusicXML "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<divisions>"},{"type":"text","text":" element."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLAttributes/divisions":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAttributes\/divisions","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"divisions"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL20MXLPositiveDivisionsV","text":"MXLPositiveDivisions"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlattributes\/divisions","role":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Musical notation duration is commonly represented as fractions. The divisions element indicates how many"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"divisions per quarter note are used to indicate a note’s duration. For example, if duration = 1 and divisions"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"= 2, this is an eighth note duration. Duration and divisions are used directly for generating sound output, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"they must be chosen to take tuplets into account. Using a divisions element lets us use just one number to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"represent a duration for each note in the score, while retaining the full power of a fractional"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"representation. If maximum compatibility with Standard MIDI 1.0 files is important, do not have the divisions"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value exceed 16383."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"divisions"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLAttributes":{"title":"MXLAttributes","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlattributes","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The attributes element contains musical information that typically changes on measure boundaries. This"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"includes key and time signatures, clefs, transpositions, and staving. When attributes are changed mid-measure,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it affects the music in score order, not in MusicXML document order."}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLAttributes","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLAttributes","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAttributes"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPositiveDivisions":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLPositiveDivisions","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLPositiveDivisions","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlpositivedivisions","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPositiveDivisions","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLPositiveDivisions","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The positive-divisions type restricts divisions values to positive numbers."}]}}}